  "unit_note": "USD millions. '......' (No Transactions) and '(**)' (less than $500,000 in absolute value) cells are omitted, not transcribed as 0. Columns are three period groups of Gross Outlays / Applicable Receipts / Outlays(net); the declared identities are Outlays(net) + Applicable = Gross on the total row where all three print, and a section roll-up per column over the rows that print in it. August prints the This-Month Applicable Receipts total as '(**)' (July printed 1) and omits every Intrabudgetary Transactions cell, so the This-Month net identity has only one declarable source and is not declared: 8 relations against the provisional floor of 9 is a printed-cell omission, not padding. The all-omitted Intrabudgetary Transactions row is dropped (family convention, as #429 dropped its all-omitted row), so the total is row 6. Roles are graph-consistent per the U1 finding: the total-row Applicable Receipts cells that feed the net identities (r6c5, r6c8) are leaf, not the July twin's standalone marking; only the two proprietary-receipts applicable cells that feed no declarable relation are standalone.",
